between the chocolate peanut butter the  chocolate caramel it makes for the  ultimate dessert i'm natalie potter and  i'm laura potter we're bliss and baker  and we're back at tasty to share our  halloween inspired rice krispie treat i  remember being a little kid and having  all this leftover candy weeks and weeks  later and so incorporating all that  leftover candy into our favorite dessert  is the perfect solution we're using the  standard crispy treat recipe with just a  touch of vanilla so that your favorite  candies can be the star of the show we  recommend using your favorite chocolate  candy over something gummy or sour  because we feel like it just complements  the rice krispies treat better so we're  going to start with the salted butter in  a non-stick pot or in this case a  cauldron once the butter is melted pour  in the mini marshmallows and just stir  it occasionally until they're all  completely melted it's really important  to melt the mini marshmallows on low to  prevent them from burning we prefer to  use the mini marshmallows over the large  ones because they melt much faster and  more evenly now it's time to add the  cereal and fold to combine seriously  this is my favorite part i love to see  it all come together now we're scooping  half the mixture into a prepared pan and  you really want to try to cover the  entire bottom of the pan so that the  candy doesn't fall through we think this  is the perfect recipe to make with your  kids post trick-or-treating and it's a  great way to get your kids to share  their candy with you we love this recipe  because of the contrast between the  vanilla and the chocolate and now you  can sprinkle your favorite chocolate  candies on top now we're going to spread  the rest of the mixture on top you can  use a spatula or even a little bit of  nonstick spray on your hands after we  chopped our chocolate we put it in the  freezer for a bit so it wouldn't melt  into the warm rice krispie treat mixture  as if there 